IMPORT prelude

-- Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955 (Singapore) -- how long the Act lasts (s 1(2)); illegal strikes and lock-outs in
-- essential services (ss 6 to 11, First Schedule Part 1); dispersal of assemblies (s 13); failure to report scheduled offences
-- (s 16, Second Schedule); arrestability and District Court sentencing limits (ss 18, 20, 21); consent to body samples (ss 27,
-- 27A); detention and police supervision orders (ss 30, 31, 33(3), 35, Fourth Schedule); detention of suspects (s 44).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CLTPA1955.txt (SSO
-- "Current version as at 01 Oct 2026"), with amendments to Act 18 of 2024 (in force 21 October 2024) shown, and an Act 3 of 2021
-- amendment to the Second Schedule in force 1 July 2025.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 6 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules with decision content that
-- a person, employer, union or practitioner meets. Not encoded: the supplies and subversive-document offences of ss 3 and 4 beyond
-- their maximum terms, search and boarding powers (s 14), evidence and trial rules (ss 22 to 25), retention of samples (s 27C),
-- advisory committees and the President's confirmation (ss 31(2), (3), 38 to 41), conditions of detention and temporary release
-- (ss 42, 43), arrest powers (ss 45 to 47), and the notice forms in First Schedule Part 2. Strikes illegal under "any other written
-- law" (s 7) are not modelled.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Criminal Law (Temporary Provisions) Act 1955`

§§ `1(2) -- a temporary Act, renewed`

-- s 1(2): "This Act continues in force for a period of 5 years starting on 21 October 2024." [Act 18 of 2024 wef 21/10/2024]
-- (3): expiry does not affect things previously done. Dates are written as yyyymmdd numbers. Reading the period as ending at the
-- close of 20 October 2029 is an INFERENCE from "5 years starting on".
GIVEN `the date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act is in force on` IF
    `the date` AT LEAST 20241021 AND `the date` LESS THAN 20291021

§§ `5, 6, First Schedule Part 1 -- essential services`

-- s 5: "essential service" means any service ... "included in Part 1 of the First Schedule". The Schedule lists 31 items, among
-- them banking (1), broadcasting (2), electricity and gas (7), newspaper services (11), private and public health services (16),
-- public transport and air transport (17), water services (26). A few are given here; everything else is outside Part 3.
DECLARE Service IS ONE OF
    `water services`
    `gas services`
    `electricity services`
    `banking services`
    `public transport services`
    `newspaper services`
    `a private hospital`
    `a restaurant`
    `a retail shop`

GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the service is essential` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `a restaurant` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a retail shop` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6(1): "No workman employed in any of the following essential services shall go on strike: (a) water services; (b) gas
-- services; (c) electricity services." (3): no employer shall lock out any workman in those services. No notice cures it.
GIVEN `the service` IS A Service
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stoppages are banned outright` IF
    CONSIDER `the service`
    WHEN `water services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `gas services` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `electricity services` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `6 to 8 -- illegal strikes and lock-outs`

-- s 6(2): in any other essential service, no workman shall strike "(a) unless at least 14 days before striking he has given to
-- his employer notice of intention to strike as provided by this section; (b) before the date of striking specified in the
-- notice ...; or (c) during the pendency of any proceedings". (4): the same for an employer's lock-out.
-- (5): the strike notice must be delivered to the employer or manager and "signed by not less than 7 workmen ... or by 7
-- representatives of the trade union", in Form 1. (6): the lock-out notice must be signed by the employer and delivered to a
-- representative of the workmen or a union officer, in Form 2.
-- (9): "Every notice ... shall expire at the end of 30 days from the date of the notice."
-- (10): "proceedings" are conciliation, Industrial Arbitration Court or board-of-inquiry proceedings under the Industrial
-- Relations Act 1960.
-- s 7: a strike or lock-out "commenced, declared or continued in contravention of section 6" is illegal.
-- s 8: "A lock-out declared in consequence of an illegal strike or a strike declared in consequence of an illegal lock-out shall
-- not be deemed to be illegal."
--
-- `days of notice` counts the days from the date of the notice to the start of the stoppage (0 if no notice). A stoppage that
-- starts more than 30 days after the notice starts on an expired notice: that reading of s 6(9) together with s 6(2)(a) is an
-- INFERENCE. The duties to copy the notice to the Commissioner within 3 days (s 6(8)) and to post a lock-out notice at 3 places
-- (s 6(7)) are not treated as conditions of legality. Use of the prescribed Form is folded into "delivered as required".
DECLARE Kind IS ONE OF `a strike`, `a lock-out`

DECLARE Stoppage HAS
    `kind` IS A Kind
    `service` IS A Service
    `days of notice` IS A NUMBER
    `signatories` IS A NUMBER
    `signed by the employer` IS A BOOLEAN
    `delivered as required` IS A BOOLEAN
    `starts before the date in the notice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proceedings pending` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in answer to an illegal stoppage by the other side` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the stoppage` IS A Stoppage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is properly signed` IF
    CONSIDER `the stoppage`'s `kind`
    WHEN `a strike` THEN `the stoppage`'s `signatories` AT LEAST 7
    WHEN `a lock-out` THEN `the stoppage`'s `signed by the employer`

GIVEN `the stoppage` IS A Stoppage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is valid` IF
        `the stoppage`'s `days of notice` AT LEAST 14
    AND `the stoppage`'s `days of notice` AT MOST 30
    AND `the notice is properly signed` `the stoppage`
    AND `the stoppage`'s `delivered as required`

GIVEN `the stoppage` IS A Stoppage
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the stoppage is illegal` IF
        `the service is essential` (`the stoppage`'s `service`)
    AND (NOT `the stoppage`'s `in answer to an illegal stoppage by the other side`)
    AND (    `stoppages are banned outright` (`the stoppage`'s `service`)
          OR (NOT `the notice is valid` `the stoppage`)
          OR `the stoppage`'s `starts before the date in the notice`
          OR `the stoppage`'s `proceedings pending`
        )

§§ `9 to 13, 16, 20, 21, 27A, 33 -- offences, penalties and courts`

-- s 9(1) workman in an illegal strike; (2) employer in an illegal lock-out; s 10 instigating; s 11 "knowingly expends or applies
-- any money in direct furtherance or support of any illegal strike or lock-out": each "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or ... both".
-- s 3(1) demanding supplies for those acting against public safety: 10 years. s 4(1) making or possessing a subversive document:
-- 10 years. s 13(2) joining an assembly ordered to disperse: $1,000 or 6 months. s 16(1) failing to report: 5 years.
-- s 27A(4)(a) refusing photographs, finger impressions or samples without reasonable excuse: $1,000 or one month.
-- s 33(3) breaching a supervision obligation: "imprisonment for a term of not less than one year and not more than 3 years".
-- s 14(4) obstructing a search: "shall be guilty of an offence", with no penalty stated; s 20 gives the general penalty, "$5,000
-- or ... 3 years or ... both", "subject to any special provisions". Applying s 20 to s 14(4) is an INFERENCE.
-- A fine of 0 below means the section states no fine.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `taking part in an illegal strike`
    `an illegal lock-out`
    `instigating an illegal strike`
    `financing an illegal strike`
    `demanding supplies for those acting against public safety`
    `possessing a subversive document`
    `joining an assembly ordered to disperse`
    `failing to report a scheduled offence`
    `refusing to give finger impressions`
    `breaching a supervision obligation`
    `obstructing a search`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal strike` THEN 2000
    WHEN `an illegal lock-out` THEN 2000
    WHEN `instigating an illegal strike` THEN 2000
    WHEN `financing an illegal strike` THEN 2000
    WHEN `joining an assembly ordered to disperse` THEN 1000
    WHEN `refusing to give finger impressions` THEN 1000
    WHEN `obstructing a search` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal strike` THEN 12
    WHEN `an illegal lock-out` THEN 12
    WHEN `instigating an illegal strike` THEN 12
    WHEN `financing an illegal strike` THEN 12
    WHEN `demanding supplies for those acting against public safety` THEN 120
    WHEN `possessing a subversive document` THEN 120
    WHEN `joining an assembly ordered to disperse` THEN 6
    WHEN `failing to report a scheduled offence` THEN 60
    WHEN `refusing to give finger impressions` THEN 1
    WHEN `breaching a supervision obligation` THEN 36
    WHEN `obstructing a search` THEN 36

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the minimum imprisonment in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `breaching a supervision obligation` THEN 12
    OTHERWISE 0

-- s 18: "Every offence under this Act, other than an offence under section 9, shall be arrestable and non-bailable".
-- So the striking workman and the locking-out employer may be bailed, but the person who instigates or finances the strike may not.
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is arrestable and non-bailable` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `taking part in an illegal strike` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an illegal lock-out` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 21: a District Court may try any offence under this Act "and ... impose therefor a fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment
-- for a term not exceeding 5 years or both". [40/2019]
GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a District Court can impose the full maximum` IF
        `the maximum fine` `the offence` AT MOST 5000
    AND `the maximum imprisonment in months` `the offence` AT MOST 60

§§ `13 -- dispersal of assemblies`

-- s 13(1): when the Minister declares "an immediate threat to public peace", a police officer "not below the rank of sergeant"
-- may command "any assembly of 10 or more persons" to disperse; (2) joining or continuing in it is an offence; (3) a declaration
-- remains in force "for a period not exceeding 48 hours" (a further declaration may be made).
GIVEN `hours since the declaration` IS A NUMBER, `commanded by a sergeant or above` IS A BOOLEAN, `persons assembled` IS A NUMBER, `stayed or joined after the command` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `staying in the assembly is an offence` IF
        `hours since the declaration` AT MOST 48
    AND `commanded by a sergeant or above`
    AND `persons assembled` AT LEAST 10
    AND `stayed or joined after the command`

§§ `16, Second Schedule -- failing to report`

-- s 16(1): a person who, "knowing or having reasonable cause to believe" another is guilty of a Second Schedule offence, "fails to
-- report the same to a police officer at the earliest possible opportunity" commits an offence: 5 years. (2): the burden of
-- proving there was no opportunity, or that a report was made at the earliest possible opportunity, "shall lie on the accused".
-- (3): not communications from client to advocate and solicitor protected under s 128 of the Evidence Act 1893.
-- Second Schedule: Arms Offences Act 1973 ss 3, 6 and 7; Corrosive and Explosive Substances and Offensive Weapons Act 1958 "Section
-- 3 or 4 involving an explosive substance". Nothing else.
DECLARE Crime IS ONE OF
    `an Arms Offences Act section 3, 6 or 7 offence`
    `a section 3 or 4 offence involving an explosive substance`
    `a section 3 or 4 offence involving only a corrosive substance`
    `a robbery`
    `a murder`

GIVEN `the crime` IS A Crime
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the crime must be reported` IF
    CONSIDER `the crime`
    WHEN `an Arms Offences Act section 3, 6 or 7 offence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a section 3 or 4 offence involving an explosive substance` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the crime` IS A Crime, `knew or had reasonable cause to believe` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved a report at the earliest opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved there was no opportunity` IS A BOOLEAN, `learned it as a client's privileged communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `not reporting is an offence` IF
        `the crime must be reported` `the crime`
    AND `knew or had reasonable cause to believe`
    AND (NOT `proved a report at the earliest opportunity`)
    AND (NOT `proved there was no opportunity`)
    AND (NOT `learned it as a client's privileged communication`)

§§ `27, 27A -- body samples`

-- s 27(1) "appropriate consent": (a) 16 and above, the person's written consent; (b) 14 and above but below 16, the written consent
-- of "both that person and of his parent or guardian"; (c) below 14, the parent's or guardian's.
-- s 27A(5): no "(a) sample of blood; or (b) invasive sample" shall be taken "unless the appropriate consent is given". Other
-- samples (head hair, mouth swab) and photographs and finger impressions must be submitted to (27A(3)), and reasonable force may be
-- used (27A(4)(b)).
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `the person consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent or guardian consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `appropriate consent is given` IF
    IF `age` AT LEAST 16
    THEN `the person consents in writing`
    ELSE IF `age` AT LEAST 14
         THEN (`the person consents in writing` AND `a parent or guardian consents in writing`)
         ELSE `a parent or guardian consents in writing`

DECLARE Sample IS ONE OF `a blood sample`, `a mouth swab`, `head hair with roots`, `finger impressions`

GIVEN `the sample` IS A Sample, `age` IS A NUMBER, `the person consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent or guardian consents in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sample may be taken` IF
    CONSIDER `the sample`
    WHEN `a blood sample` THEN `appropriate consent is given` `age` `the person consents in writing` `a parent or guardian consents in writing`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `30, 31, Fourth Schedule -- detention and supervision orders`

-- s 30(1): where the Minister is satisfied a person "has been associated with activities of a criminal nature", the Minister may,
-- "with the consent of the Public Prosecutor", (a) order detention "for any period not exceeding 12 months", or (b) police
-- supervision "for any period not exceeding 3 years". (2): "Every decision of the Minister ... is final." (3): activities of a
-- criminal nature are those in the Fourth Schedule: unlicensed moneylending, drug trafficking, secret society or gangster
-- involvement, human trafficking, robbery with firearms, murder, gang rape, kidnapping, organised crime, and attempts, abetment
-- and conspiracy. s 31(1): the order must be referred to an advisory committee "within 28 days".
DECLARE Activity IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed moneylending`
    `drug trafficking`
    `secret society involvement`
    `robbery with firearms`
    `robbery without firearms`
    `cheating`

DECLARE OrderKind IS ONE OF `detention`, `police supervision`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the activity is of a criminal nature` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `robbery without firearms` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `cheating` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the order kind` IS A OrderKind
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the longest order in months` IS
    CONSIDER `the order kind`
    WHEN `detention` THEN 12
    WHEN `police supervision` THEN 36

GIVEN `the activity` IS A Activity, `the Public Prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN, `the order kind` IS A OrderKind, `months ordered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister may make the order` IF
        `the activity is of a criminal nature` `the activity`
    AND `the Public Prosecutor consents`
    AND `months ordered` AT MOST `the longest order in months` `the order kind`

GIVEN `days since the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `referral to the advisory committee is in time` IF
    `days since the order` AT MOST 28

§§ `35 -- double penalties`

-- s 35: a person subject to supervision convicted of an offence "committed after the date of the order" under a Third Schedule law
-- is liable to "a term twice as long as the maximum term for which he would otherwise have been liable ... and also to caning".
-- The Third Schedule lists parts of the Arms Offences, Corrosive and Explosive Substances, Hostage-Taking, Internal Security,
-- Kidnapping, Misuse of Drugs and Societies Acts and a list of Penal Code sections.
GIVEN `under supervision` IS A BOOLEAN, `committed after the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `under a Third Schedule law` IS A BOOLEAN, `ordinary maximum in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum term in months` IS
    IF `under supervision` AND `committed after the order` AND `under a Third Schedule law`
    THEN `ordinary maximum in months` TIMES 2
    ELSE `ordinary maximum in months`

§§ `44 -- detaining a suspect pending enquiries`

-- s 44(1): any police officer may arrest without warrant and detain pending enquiries a person he believes could be detained under
-- s 30(1). (2): not "for a period exceeding 24 hours except with the authority of a police officer of or above the rank of
-- assistant superintendent or for a period of 48 hours in all". (3): an officer "of or above the rank of superintendent" may
-- authorise further detention "for an additional period not exceeding 14 days". Superintendent authority is assumed here to come
-- on top of the 48 hours (INFERENCE from "additional").
GIVEN `authorised by an assistant superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN, `authorised by a superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the longest detention in hours` IS
    IF `authorised by a superintendent`
    THEN 48 PLUS (14 TIMES 24)
    ELSE IF `authorised by an assistant superintendent`
         THEN 48
         ELSE 24
